    "q-75503": {
      "dom_id": "step-q75503",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only\".",
