    "q-131369": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131369",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following matrices are transformed into the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix after applying the row operations ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{1}↔{R}_{2}?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply the operations to each of the matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -24 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times  \\\\ B & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =I\\,✓ \\\\ C & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -24\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -24 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne I\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only\".",
