    "q-31944": {
      "dom_id": "step-q31944",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "The inverse of the $2\\times 2$ matrix $P$ is found using row operations, as shown below. Complete the process, and determine ${P}^{-1}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[P\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{5}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{3}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}} & \\bbox[2pt,lightgray]{\\phantom{a}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "We write down $P$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $P$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[P\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{5}{3} & \\frac{2}{3} & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{3}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{5} & \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 0 & 1 & \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${P}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{P}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5} & \\frac{1}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
